5.94.m:
With what reason in view did you come to have [such] names?"
The ghosts said:
"Delicious food was always eaten by me, but stale food was given to a twice-born;

And whatever your wish to ask, ask other things; I shall tell you."
The brahmin said:
"Whatever living beings dwell upon the earth are all dependent on food;

5.95.m:
He who worships Hari in this manner obtains the yoga of devotion.

That body which is white with the dust of bowing to Kṛṣṇa is truly auspicious;
by austerity those two eyes are acquired, charmingly beautiful, with which Hari is beheld.
